==In popular culture==
{{Main|Cultural impact of Star Wars{{!}}Cultural impact of ''Star Wars''}}

Since the release of ''The Phantom Menace'', Maul has proven to be a popular character.<ref name=":0" /> Whilst the movie received a mixed reaction from fans and critics alike, the character was one of the most highly praised parts of the film, despite his limited screen time. ''[[IGN]]'' named Maul the 16th greatest ''Star Wars'' character, noting, "Of the countless characters to walk in and out of the ''Star Wars'' saga, none looks or acts more badass than Maul."<ref name="ign">{{cite web |title=Darth Maul- #16 |url=http://www.ign.com/star-wars-characters/16.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120529123632/http://www.ign.com/star-wars-characters/16.html |archive-date=May 29, 2012 |access-date=June 13, 2012 |publisher=Ign.com}}</ref> C-3PO actor [[Anthony Daniels]] said in his memoirs that Darth Maul is still one of his favourite characters in the saga - despite his brief appearance in ''The Phantom Menace''.{{sfn |Daniels |2019 |p=168}}

Maul-related merchandise was popular among [[Hasbro]] ''Star Wars'' toy lines, with plastic recreations of his double bladed lightsaber and various action figures in his likeness developed. Maul was the focal point of the marketing campaign surrounding the [[2012 in film|2012]] re-release of ''The Phantom Menace'', being featured on the packaging for the toy line.<ref name="merch">{{cite web |title=Star Wars Crafts and Creativity - StarWars.com |url=https://www.starwars.com/vault/collecting/2012_star_wars_line_look/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110902013616/http://www.starwars.com/vault/collecting/2012_star_wars_line_look/index.html |archive-date=September 2, 2011 |access-date=November 10, 2017 |website=StarWars.com}}</ref>

Darth Maul appears as a skater in ''[[Tony Hawk's Pro Skater 3]]'' being earned for completing all 54 goals and gaining all gold medals as Tony Hawk.<ref>{{cite web |last=McDonnell |first=Jess |date=May 11, 2022 |title=10 Craziest Hidden Characters In Video Games |url=https://whatculture.com/gaming/10-craziest-hidden-characters-in-video-games-2 |access-date=December 18, 2024 |website=whatculture.com}}</ref>

===''Darth Maul'' fan film===
{{Main|Darth Maul: Apprentice{{!}}''Darth Maul: Apprentice''}}

A Maul fan film titled ''[[Darth Maul: Apprentice]]'' was released on [[YouTube]] on March 5, 2016. Darth Maul is played by Ben Shammas.<ref>{{cite web |date=March 5, 2016 |title=DARTH MAUL: Apprenti - Un Fan-Film de Star Wars |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Djo_91jN3Pk |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230822141753/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Djo_91jN3Pk |archive-date=August 22, 2023 |access-date=August 30, 2023 |website=[[YouTube]]}}</ref>

==="Darth Maul kids" viral videos===
{{Main|Star Wars Kid{{!}}''Star Wars Kid''}}

At least two videos of people trying to imitate Darth Maul have gone viral: the 2003 ''[[Star Wars Kid]]'', which spawned an [[internet meme]], and another which went [[viral video|viral]] in December 2017 of an 8-year-old [[Ontario]] boy pretending to be Darth Maul and displaying his martial arts skills.<ref>{{cite web |date=December 7, 2017 |title=Eight year old karate kid goes viral with Darth Maul skills |url=https://www.ctvnews.ca/canada/article/eight-year-old-karate-kid-goes-viral-with-darth-maul-skills/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180708074445/https://www.ctvnews.ca/canada/eight-year-old-karate-kid-goes-viral-with-darth-maul-skills-1.3711625 |archive-date=July 8, 2018 |access-date=July 8, 2018 |work=[[CTV News]]}}</ref>

